window.docContents[130].resolve({"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementComposed/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementComposed":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Session › StatementComposed.leanTier 2 · definitions\n\nTier 2 · definitions used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 437 of 545 lines trusted trust banner B3, trusted in part source ↗Read the definitions shown. Only the declarations that the headline statements use are shown, with the namespace, section, open and variable commands needed to read them. The collapsed runs are theorems, which Lean checks, and definitions that no headline statement uses.\n\nDeclarations on this page (32)def Encaps1Totalstructure RefuseStatedef onSenddef onAcceptdef onDeliverabbrev RefuseMdef refuseTransmitdef refuseChalldef refuseDeliverdef refuseInjectdef refuseCorrdef refuseCorrB0Impldef refuseCorrB0def prefixPrgAvgdef prefixPrfAvgdef prefixWireAvgdef prefixAdvAvgstructure SessionCostedReductionsdef sessionCostedReductionsBoundeddef fsAeadSlotSumBounddef fsChainPrgMixtureTermdef fsSaltWireMixtureTermdef fsAeadMixtureBounddef refineConstdef eps0IdealUnitdef hiddenSaltMixtureBounddef fig8MixShortAuthV1def fig8MixShortPrivV1def uniformStartMixtureBoundabbrev SessionCostedReductionFamilydef SessionCostedReductionFamilyBoundeddef DhKerUniform\n\nSession-level bound terms, adversary wrapper and reduction bundles shared by the statementsTrusted in part. The theorems of Computational/Theorems/ use every definition in this file except paramsV1, which is checked by Lean; the ones they use are part of what you must read to trust the result. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Assembles the single-session security bound (uniformStartMixtureBound) for the Double Ratchet with SPQR V1 (paramsV1) from the ACD19 (Alwen, Coretti, Dodis, EUROCRYPT 2019) Fig. 8 authenticity and privacy bounds (fig8MixShortAuthV1, fig8MixShortPrivV1, fsAeadMixtureBound), the session-to-Fig. 8 refinement slack (refineConst, hiddenSaltMixtureBound; DEV-LS36), and the epoch-0 and uniform-start root-KDF PRG switches (eps0IdealUnit). Also defines the early-corruption refusal wrapper RefuseB0.refuseCorrB0 (DEV-LS33, DEV-LS34), ML-KEM encapsulation totality (Encaps1Total), and scalar-independent DH equality fibers (DhKerUniform).Bounds are stated over a context mixture oa : ProbComp α via prefixPrgAvg, prefixPrfAvg, prefixWireAvg, and prefixAdvAvg, and evaluated on first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction bundles (SessionCostedReductions, sessionCostedReductionsBounded; see Computational/docs/REDUCTION_DSL_TUTORIAL.md).\n\n\n\nML-KEM encapsulation totality\n\ndef Encaps1TotalL55–59 ↗#K.encaps1 succeeds on every 64-byte header (satisfied by libcrux ML-KEM-768, which checks only header length).\n\n\n\nstructure RefuseStateL65–70 ↗#Observable game-state shadow tracked by refuseCorrB0: party epochs, within-epoch indices, and in-transit (pos, ct) pairs.\n\n\n\ndef onSendL76–84 ↗#Updates RefuseState after an accepted transmit or chall returning some c.\n\ndef onAcceptL86–90 ↗#Updates RefuseState when P accepts a message at position pos.\n\ndef onDeliverL92–96 ↗#Updates RefuseState after an accepted deliver-P(c).\n\n\n\nabbrev RefuseML100 ↗#\n\ndef refuseTransmitL102–111 ↗#\n\ndef refuseChallL113–122 ↗#\n\ndef refuseDeliverL124–133 ↗#\n\ndef refuseInjectL135–144 ↗#\n\ndef refuseCorrL146–155 ↗#Locally refuses corr-B when epoch .B == 0 (DEV-LS33) or epoch .A < 10 (DEV-LS34), and forwards all other corruption queries.\n\ndef refuseCorrB0ImplL157–171 ↗#\n\ndef refuseCorrB0L173–177 ↗#Wraps A so that corr-B queries refused by noBobCorrInEpoch0 (DEV-LS33) or noBobCorrWhileAliceBelowEpoch10 (DEV-LS34) return none without querying the game.\n\n\n\nMixture averaging and SPQR V1 session bound\n\ndef prefixPrgAvgL183–185 ↗#Averages a family of PRG distinguishers D o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixPrfAvgL187–192 ↗#Averages a family of PRF adversaries D o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixWireAvgL194–199 ↗#Averages a family of wire OT-CCA adversaries A o over a prefix distribution oa.\n\ndef prefixAdvAvgL201–204 ↗#Averages a family of adversaries in an arbitrary game with coins unifSpec.\n\nstructure SessionCostedReductionsL206–283 ↗#Bundle of first-order ReductionDsl.CostedReduction programs for a single Double Ratchet + SPQR V1 session at send coins BitVec 512. Combines the SPK (spk), ACD19 Fig. 8 (fig8), and FS-AEAD (fs) reduction bundles with the session-to-Fig. 8 simulators, root-KDF PRG distinguishers, and DeliverForge authenticity reductions. ML-KEM encapsulation and decapsulation failures are excluded here and charged via MlKem.KemFailBad on the universally quantified adversary, since an existentially quantified reduction could hard-code a failing seed pair.\n\ndef sessionCostedReductionsBoundedL285–326 ↗#Step-cost, program-size, and oracle-query bounds for all reductions in R at query budget q, epoch bound qep, and cost budget ratchetCostBudget q (qep + 1). Also imposes semantic query bounds min (2 + 2 * q) (q + 3) on R.B_prng and min (2 * q) (q + 2) on R.B_fs.\n\ndef fsAeadSlotSumBoundL328–337 ↗#Per-session computational FS-AEAD deliver-forgery bound on R across the fsSlotCount qR active slots (chain-PRG, twice salt-PRF, and wire OT-CCA).\n\ndef fsChainPrgMixtureTermL339–347 ↗#Mixture-averaged chain-PRG advantage at hybrid hop m and query fuel qR.\n\ndef fsSaltWireMixtureTermL349–366 ↗#Mixture-averaged salt-PRF and wire OT-CCA advantage terms at hybrid hop m and query fuel qR.\n\ndef fsAeadMixtureBoundL368–378 ↗#Mixture-averaged FS-AEAD short bound across fsSlotCount q active slots plus the hoisted MAC-forgery term 4 * qd * macForgeryProb C.F.\n\n1 declaration not shown (lines 380–383): theorems, which Lean checks, or definitions that no headline statement usesCryptoVerification.E2E.paramsV1\n\ndef refineConstL385–390 ↗#Context-independent session-to-Fig. 8 refinement slack: spurious DH-step terms plus the ratchet-key collision bound (qep + 2) * (q + qep + 2) * δ.\n\ndef eps0IdealUnitL392–397 ↗#Worst-case probability that uniform PRG output passes wireMacVerifiesTest, over chain counters c < 2 ^ 32 and wire lengths ser.length < 2 ^ 32 (DEV-LS23).\n\ndef hiddenSaltMixtureBoundL399–437 ↗#Mixture upper bound on the hidden-salt refinement probe game when SPQR lacks salt binding (DEV-LS36). Integrates the DeliverForge CKA, PRF-PRNG, FS-AEAD, and MAC-forgery bounds over o ← oa, plus spuriousStepTerm (for forward-evicted honest wires probed after sender corruption) and (qep + 1) * (qep + 2) * δ. Excludes ML-KEM failure probabilities, which are charged at top level via the real-game bad event MlKem.KemFailBad on the universally quantified adversary.\n\ndef fig8MixShortAuthV1L439–459 ↗#Mixture-averaged ACD19 Fig. 8 authenticity bound for (R o).simFig8 on SPQR V1, with FS-AEAD terms expanded via fsAeadMixtureBound.\n\ndef fig8MixShortPrivV1L461–482 ↗#Mixture-averaged ACD19 Fig. 8 privacy bound for (R o).simFig8 on SPQR V1, with FS-AEAD terms expanded via fsAeadMixtureBound.\n\ndef uniformStartMixtureBoundL484–508 ↗#Upper bound on the mixture-averaged sessionSchemeU game bias with SPQR V1 on RefuseB0.refuseCorrB0-wrapped adversaries: sums the ACD19 Fig. 8 authenticity and privacy bounds, refineConst, the epoch-0 and uniform-start rootKdfAsPrg advantages, and 2 * hiddenSaltMixtureBound.\n\nParameterized reduction families and DH kernel hypothesis\n\nabbrev SessionCostedReductionFamilyL512–520 ↗#Family of SessionCostedReductions bundles indexed by cryptographic primitives, identity keys, group encoding, and query budgets (qep, q).\n\ndef SessionCostedReductionFamilyBoundedL522–530 ↗#Uniform resource boundedness (sessionCostedReductionsBounded) across all parameter instantiations of D.\n\ndef DhKerUniformL532–546 ↗#Scalar-independence of DH equality fibers (Dh.dh x Q = Dh.dh x Q' ↔ Dh.dh s Q = Dh.dh s Q'), used in hop 2 to relabel the epoch-0 random function across scalars.For clamped x-only X25519 on the prime-order subgroup Pt (0 plus the (ℓ - 1) / 2 pairs {±P} of order ℓ = 2 ^ 252 + 27742317777372353535851937790883648493), every clamped scalar c = 8m (2 ^ 251 ≤ m < 2 ^ 252) satisfies gcd(c, ℓ) = 1, so Q ↦ u(c · Q) is a bijection on Pt (δ = 2 ^ (-250)). The carrier Pt must be restricted to this prime-order subgroup under clamped scalars: nonzero E[8] or twist E'[4] torsion points are annihilated by 8m (which violates dh x Q ≠ 0), mixed-order or twist cosets separate uniform Pt challenges from honest basepoint multiples in CKA.corrGame, and unclamped scalars fail at x ≡ 0 (mod ℓ).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Session/StatementComposed.lean","id":"/Tier-2___-definitions/Computational___Specifications___/Computational.Specifications.Session.StatementComposed/#file-Computational___Specifications___Session___StatementComposed"}});